# UI Testing and Verification

For GUI/TUI applications, follow these standards.

## Screenshot Capability

- Include screenshot capability in all GUI/TUI apps
- For Textual apps, use built-in screenshot (`Ctrl+S` or programmatic capture)
- Document all UI states and layouts with visual examples

## Visual Regression Testing

- Implement automated tests that capture screenshots and compare against reference images
- Reference screenshots stored in `tests/screenshots/` for testing, `docs/screenshots/` for documentation
- Tests fail if UI output differs from reference screenshots (unless intentional)
- Update reference screenshots when UI changes are reviewed and approved
- For Textual apps, screenshots are SVG files (viewable and version-controllable)

## Test Types

- Use snapshot testing tools (`pytest-snapshot` or custom comparison)
- Positive tests: UI renders correctly for expected inputs
- Negative tests: errors display properly for invalid inputs

## Workflow

1. Build or modify UI component
2. Capture reference screenshot
3. Store in `tests/screenshots/`
4. Write test that renders component and compares output
5. On future changes, test detects differences automatically
6. Review and update references when changes are intentional
